# Madame Pearl, the fortune teller (worlds/01_PIER.md, Key 5). She sells Swyne's toys under the table. In the suit,
# Nim poses as a buyer for a club and has to stay in character: each "slip" flag costs Composure, and two slips or
# naming the Rope lose the sale and blow her cover (levels/pier/keys/pearl.gd). Pearl's reading is right about the
# ledger and wrong about everything else.

~ start
[if pier/pearl_sold] => after
[if not pier/in_suit] => garb
Pearl [mystic]: Sit, sit. Cross my palm and the spirits will speak.
Pearl: Your palm, or your purse? The spirits take both.
- I'm not here for the spirits. I'm here to buy. => buy
- Ooh, could you do my palm first? => palm

~ palm
set pier/pearl_slip1
Pearl: Hmm. A long life line. A short attention span. Do you want a reading, or do you want to buy something?
- To buy. And don't waste my time again. => buy
- Sorry! To buy, please. => buy_soft

~ buy_soft
set pier/pearl_slip2
=> buy

~ buy
Pearl [sly]: Buy what, dear? I sell futures.
- The prizes. The ones that hum. My club wants a crate. => crate
- Um. The... humming ones? If that's all right? => crate_soft

~ crate_soft
[if pier/pearl_slip1 or pier/pearl_slip2] => refused
set pier/pearl_slip3
=> crate

~ crate
Pearl: A club, is it. And which club would that be?
- The kind you don't ask about. => sold
- The Velvet Rope. => refused

~ refused
Pearl [cold]: Oh, I don't think you're buying anything, dear. I think you're looking. HELP! THIEVES!
set pier/pearl_refused
=> END

~ sold
Pearl [sly]: Ooh. One of those. The order goes in Laffer's little book, and the crate comes in under the boards.
Pearl [mystic]: And for you, a free reading. I see... a ledger. A little book of names, travelling somewhere it shouldn't. Somewhere with hedges.
Pearl: And I see you settling down with a nice accountant. You'll never climb anything taller than a stepladder.
Nim: One out of three.
[narrator] Under the table, a boxed plushie with a spiral on its belly. Nim takes it as a sample. Pearl doesn't argue.
set pier/pearl_sold
=> END

~ garb
Pearl: The spirits don't speak to customers who come in dripping, dear. Come back dressed for business.

~ after
Pearl [mystic]: The spirits say you've had your reading. The spirits also say no refunds.
